{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Patchset 2 pushed to change 2263 (same Change-Id If9a48b39, not a duplicate change) implementing the new system-owned-exclusion acceptance criterion.\n\nWhat changed:\n- `_SYSTEM_PATH_PREFIXES` — a documented constant chosen from the 29 measured offenders: `/System/`, `/usr/libexec/`, `/usr/sbin/`, `/usr/bin/`, `/Library/Apple/`, `/Library/Application Support/JAMF/`, plus `/sbin/` and `/usr/lib/systemd/` as the Linux analogues (noted as unobserved on this host). Deliberately excludes `/opt/homebrew/`, `/usr/local/`, `/Applications/` and `$HOME` — that is where leaked helpers live.\n- `is_system_owned(command)` — prefix match against the WHOLE command line, which anchors it to the executable. A system path appearing as an argument must not launder a user process (`/bin/bash /System/Library/x.sh` is user-space), and prefix-on-whole-string also survives the space in the JAMF path, which splitting on whitespace would not.\n- `find_orphaned_load(..., *, include_system=False)` and a `--include-system` flag.\n- Report footer states the suppressed count in both the header line and a trailing note, so the number is never silently hidden.\n- Module docstring records the 33 -> 29 -> 4 measurement and WHY PPID 1 means less on a desktop OS than the plain reading suggests.\n- AGENTS.md detector note updated to match, incl. the `--include-system` invocation.\n\nLive verification on the affected host reproduces the coordinator's measurement exactly: default reports 4 with \"(29 system-owned suppressed)\"; `--include-system` reports 33. The 4 survivors are the headroom proxy, Caffeine, logscale-collector, and `/bin/bash ~/.claude/jobs/09e12a48/tmp/watch-tracker.sh` (3.0h, PPID 1) — the genuine orphaned agent-job script the noise was burying.\n\nRED->GREEN: the 17 new assertions were appended and run first; 17 failed (missing `is_system_owned`, missing `include_system` kwarg, unfiltered behaviour). After implementing, 35/35 green. The new default also caught a latent weakness in two of my own earlier fixtures, which used `/usr/sbin/some-daemon` as a stand-in for a quiet orphan and so became system-suppressed; retargeted to `/opt/homebrew/bin/some-helper` so those tests still test the threshold.\n\nDefect-seeded mutations, all 5 killed: drop the exclusion clause -> 3 failures; `is_system_owned` always False -> 9; substring match instead of prefix (the arg-laundering hole) -> 1; suppressed count hard-coded to 0 -> 1; `--include-system` ignored -> 1.\n\nGates: make lint 0, make typecheck 0, complexity --check 0 (new=0 increased=0), check_import_walk 0, `--help` 0, 37 tests in the scripts tier, and the 290 AGENTS.md-reading tests green.\n\nNote: pushing patchset 2 removed the LLM-Review+1 that patchset 1 had earned; it needs re-review. Still not closing."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787814966593190846,"uuid":"d1fdb987-361a-46f4-b719-2cd36b251a40"}